<title>USA: Entergy sees Ark. 2 nuke on line Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Entergy sees Ark. 2 nuke on line Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Entergy Corp's 858 megawatt (MW) Arkansas 2 nuclear power unit in Russellville, Ark., will likely begin contributing to the electricity grid Tuesday, the company said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We're in the process of restarting. We should be back on line tomorrow,&quot; company spokesman Terry Young said.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, with a generating capacity of 836 MW, is operating at full power.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
</text>
